    "done_when": "reckon/crew/recovery.py classifies a run as working when its recorded worker process is alive and was launched after the manifest file's last modification, whatever terminal status that stale manifest reports. reckon/crew/obligations.py does not list such a run as promotable-stale or offer a crew complete command for it. A run whose live worker started before its manifest was written keeps today's classification. A new tests/test_a_resumed_run_counts_as_working.py drives a run with a stale complete manifest and a live worker launched after it, asserting the working classification, the w counter, and no promotion obligation. A second case covers a stale blocked manifest. A third asserts that a finished run with an exited worker still classifies as today. The declared mutation, reading the manifest status alone, fails the first case, with its log recorded including an EXIT= line. The files tests/test_recovery*.py, tests/test_crew_monitor_output.py, tests/test_crew_ticker.py, tests/test_obligations*.py and the new file show zero added failures by id against the dispatch base, with basetemp on node-local /tmp. baseline_suite and after_suite are one-line JSON with revision, tree, full command, exit_status, absolute log_path, completed, failure_count and failure_ids",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "a run whose live worker process was launched after its manifest was last written is classified as working, so the follower counts it as w and the obligation hook never offers it for promotion",
